_chemical_compound_source
;
 Treatment of 5-anthracenecarboxylic acid with oxalyl chloride yields
 5-anthracenecarboxyl chloride, which reacts with residual acid to give
 5,5'-di(anthracenecarboxylic) anhydride (1). Crystals of (1) were grown
 by the slow concentration of a dichloromethane solution.
;
